<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canning Award</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Canning Award was the 1861 arbitration by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-canning-1st-earl-canning">Lord Canning</a>, Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, of the succession dispute between the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-sultan">Sayyid Said of Oman</a>. It separated the Sultanate of Zanzibar under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majid-bin-said">Majid bin Said</a> from the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuwaini-bin-said">Thuwaini bin Said</a>, with Zanzibar paying an annual subsidy to Muscat. The award ended the unified Omani maritime empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>.</p></div>
